We know that a clockwise rotation can be represented by the matrix
$$
\left[ {\begin{array}{cc}
\cos\frac{d\pi}{180} & \sin \frac{d\pi}{180} \\
-\sin \frac{d\pi}{180} & \cos\frac{d\pi}{180}
\end{array}} \right]
$$
where $d$ represents the clockwise direction in degrees.
\begin{align*}
d&=45\\
\left[ {\begin{array}{cc}
\cos\frac{d\pi}{180} & \sin \frac{d\pi}{180} \\
-\sin \frac{d\pi}{180} & \cos\frac{d\pi}{180}
\end{array}} \right]
&=\left[ {\begin{array}{cc}
\cos\frac{45\pi}{180} & \sin \frac{45\pi}{180} \\
-\sin \frac{45\pi}{180} & \cos\frac{45\pi}{180}
\end{array}} \right]\\
&=\left[ {\begin{array}{cc}
\cos\frac{\pi}{4} & \sin \frac{\pi}{4} \\
-\sin \frac{\pi}{4} & \cos\frac{\pi}{4}
\end{array}} \right]\\
